# GitHub Pull Request Creation

When asked to create a pull request:

- Do not use `gh`. It is not expected to be available in this repository.
- Use the `user-github` MCP server for GitHub reads, searches, and duplicate checks.
- Before calling any GitHub MCP tool, list/read the matching MCP tool descriptor.
- The active `user-github` MCP server may expose only read/list/search tools. If a needed write operation is not exposed, do not stop there.
- For GitHub writes such as creating pull requests or issues, read `.cursor/mcp.json` and use the configured GitHub server token to call the GitHub REST API directly.
- Never write, print, or persist the token value in rules, docs, commits, PR bodies, or final responses.

For this repository, the standard REST API fallback is:

```powershell
$Config = Get-Content -Raw ".cursor/mcp.json" | ConvertFrom-Json
$Token = $Config.mcpServers.github.env.GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN
$Headers = @{
  Authorization = "Bearer $Token"
  Accept = "application/vnd.github+json"
  "X-GitHub-Api-Version" = "2022-11-28"
  "User-Agent" = "cursor-agent"
}

$Payload = @{
  title = "type: concise PR title"
  head = "branch-name"
  base = "master"
  body = "## Summary`n- ...`n`n## Test plan`n- ..."
} | ConvertTo-Json

Invoke-RestMethod `
  -Method Post `
  -Uri "https://api.github.com/repos/Kuboczoch/up-remastered/pulls" `
  -Headers $Headers `
  -ContentType "application/json" `
  -Body $Payload
```

Before creating, query open PRs for the same `head` and `base` to avoid duplicates.
